    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-86095",
      "publishedDate": "2026-09-04T22:38:46.036Z",
      "lastModifiedDate": "2026-09-04T22:38:46.036Z",
      "description": "Unidata netcdf-c through 4.10.1 contains an out-of-bounds write vulnerability in NC4_HDF5_inq_attname() that copies HDF5 attribute names into a fixed 256-byte buffer without length validation. Attackers can craft HDF5 files with oversized attribute names to overflow the destination buffer, causing memory corruption and crashes when applications enumerate attribute names.",
      "severity": 7.8,
      "fix_suggestion": "📦 受影响组件：Unidata netcdf-c\n🛠️ 修复建议：\n1. 确认受影响的版本范围（见上方 Affected Products）\n2. 升级到厂商官方发布的最稳定安全版本\n3. 检查官方安全公告获取补丁链接\n4. 如无法立即升级，实施临时缓解措施：\n   - 网络层：WAF 规则 / IPS 签名 / 零信任策略\n   - 主机层：最小化暴露面 / 禁用危险功能 / 输入过滤\n5. 修复后使用 NVD / 厂商 PoC 验证修复有效性",
      "references": [
        {
          "url": "https://github.com/Unidata/netcdf-c",
          "type": "reference"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://github.com/Unidata/netcdf-c/blob/v4.10.1/libhdf5/hdf5attr.c",
          "type": "reference"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/unidata-netcdf-c-through-4.10.1-out-of-bounds-write-via-oversized-hdf5-attribute-name",
          "type": "reference"
        }
      ],
      "affected": [
        {
          "vendor": "Unidata",
